{"name":"Breakaway","hex":"#cedac3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"breakaway","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having broken away from a larger unit.","Capable of breaking off without damaging the larger structure."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of breaking away from something.","A group of riders which has gone ahead of the peloton."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/breakaway"}],"entries":[{"title":"Breakaway (1955 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Breakaway is a 1955 British second feature ('B') thriller film directed by Henry Cass and starring Tom Conway, Michael Balfour and Honor Blackman. It was written by Norman Hudis based on a story by Manning O'Brine. A private eye is hot on the tail of a stolen secret formula and a kidnapped young woman. It is a sequel to Barbados Quest (1955)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Breakaway_%281955_film%29.jpg/330px-Breakaway_%281955_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakaway_(1955_film)","wikidata":"Q4959369"},{"title":"Breakaway (1966 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Breakaway is a 1966 American short film by Bruce Conner. It shows Toni Basil dancing to her song \"Breakaway\". The film has a palindromic structure in which the second half of the film reverses the image and sound of the first half. Breakaway is often cited as a precursor to the development of the music video."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakaway_(1966_film)","wikidata":"Q124614664"},{"title":"Breakaway (Kelly Clarkson song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Breakaway\" is a song recorded by American singer Kelly Clarkson. The folk-pop and pop-punk ballad, written by Matthew Gerrard, Bridget Benenate, and Avril Lavigne, was originally intended for Lavigne's debut studio album, Let Go (2002). After being deemed unsuitable for the album, it was passed to Clarkson to be recorded as a soundtrack for the film The Princess Diaries 2: Royal Engagement (2004). Clarkson, who was finishing her second studio album at that time, recorded \"Breakaway\" to tide her fans over until the first single from her new album was released. However, the song's success prompted its inclusion on Clarkson's second album, while the record label decided to name the album after the song. \"Breakaway\" was first released as the first single from The Princess Diaries 2 soundtrack on July 19, 2004. In May 2006, \"Breakaway\" was reissued as the fifth and final single from the album of the same name."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/79/Kelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_original_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakaway_(Kelly_Clarkson_song)","wikidata":"Q666168"},{"title":"Breakaway (Kelly Clarkson album)","blocks":[{"text":"Breakaway is the second studio album by American singer Kelly Clarkson, released on November 30, 2004, in Canada and in the United States, by RCA Records, with a wider release following throughout 2005. Despite the commercial success of Clarkson's debut album Thankful (2003), music critics still continued to typecast her as an American Idol winner and were also critical of her attempts of establishing a commercial appeal on her own. Wanting to stray from those, she collaborated with a range of new songwriters and producers such as Dr. Luke, Max Martin, John Shanks, Kara DioGuardi, and with former Evanescence members Ben Moody and David Hodges. This overhaul also led her to part ways with her manager Simon Fuller and hire the management services of Jeff Kwatinetz before the album's release."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/56/Breakaway_Album.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breakaway_(Kelly_Clarkson_album)","wikidata":"Q1026394"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Toni_Basil_2.jpg/500px-Toni_Basil_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Toni_Basil_2.jpg/500px-Toni_Basil_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Breakaway stars Toni Basil (pictured in 2016).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToni_Basil_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b9/Breakaway_Single.jpg/330px-Breakaway_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b9/Breakaway_Single.jpg/330px-Breakaway_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreakaway_Single.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Avril_Lavigne_playing_guitar%2C_St._Petersburg_%28crop%29.jpg/500px-Avril_Lavigne_playing_guitar%2C_St._Petersburg_%28crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Avril_Lavigne_playing_guitar%2C_St._Petersburg_%28crop%29.jpg/500px-Avril_Lavigne_playing_guitar%2C_St._Petersburg_%28crop%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Avril Lavigne co-wrote the song.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAvril_Lavigne_playing_guitar%2C_St._Petersburg_(crop).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/56/Breakaway_Screenshot.jpg/330px-Breakaway_Screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/56/Breakaway_Screenshot.jpg/330px-Breakaway_Screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clarkson attending the movie premiere of The Princess Diaries 2: Royal Engagement, as depicted in the music video.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreakaway_Screenshot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/38/Kelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_special_edition_cover.jpg/250px-Kelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_special_edition_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/38/Kelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_special_edition_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/38/Kelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_special_edition_cover.jpg/250px-Kelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_special_edition_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKelly_Clarkson_Breakaway_special_edition_cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Kelly_Clarkson_in_Canberra%2C_2005.jpg/330px-Kelly_Clarkson_in_Canberra%2C_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Kelly_Clarkson_in_Canberra%2C_2005.jpg/330px-Kelly_Clarkson_in_Canberra%2C_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clarkson performing at the Breakaway Tour in Canberra, Australia in 2005","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKelly_Clarkson_in_Canberra%2C_2005.jpg"}],"sounds":{"breakaway":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-breakaway.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/22/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-breakaway.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-breakaway.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbi